    "description": "Release step, after the slack-length and fpmax fit: the slack lengths stay, and only the fpmax of these extensors is refit. Without it they sit at the fpmax floor and nothing but joint springs opens digits 3-5 when the wrist flexes. Lower bound: the smallest common fpmax at which, in tenodesis trial B of McFarland et al. 2023 (wrist from 60 deg extension to 60 deg flexion at 20 deg/s, all muscles at act = 0; scripts/validate_hand_function.py), the MCP of each listed digit extends by at least min_mcp_extension_deg (the lower edge of the protocol's MCP range-of-motion band, mirrored). Above the bound the fpmax are set by the same one-sided joint loss. Every joint_targets row records its maximum excess without this step (fit.max_excess_Nm_without_release): the price of the release is extension moment beyond the measured totals.",
